# Cline Configuration — ExamTrust

> This file acts as a Cline adapter for ExamTrust. All authoritative engineering standards, branching models, and verification protocols are defined in `AGENTS.md` and `.agents/rules/`.

## 1. Authoritative Rules Reference
Always follow the core rules defined at:
- **Root Guidelines**: [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md)
- **Core Principles**: [.agents/rules/core.md](.agents/rules/core.md)
- **Git Flow & Boundaries**: [.agents/rules/git-workflow.md](.agents/rules/git-workflow.md)
- **Risk-Based Verification**: [.agents/rules/verification.md](.agents/rules/verification.md)
- **Security & Tool Logic Hard-Lock**: [.agents/rules/security.md](.agents/rules/security.md)

## 2. Knowledge Graph Query-First Workflow
Before broad repository searches or multi-file edits, query the Graphify knowledge graph first:
```bash
graphify query "<task description>"
```
- Use Graphify for navigation only. Source code remains the source of truth.
- After modifying code files, keep the graph synchronized with:
```bash
npx graphify hook-rebuild
```

## 3. Isolated Diagnostics Protocol
When investigating complex errors, failing tests, or runtime crashes:
- Follow the scientific debugging methodology in [`.agents/skills/diagnostics/SKILL.md`](.agents/skills/diagnostics/SKILL.md).
- Keep investigation strictly read-only and structured into the 9-part `DIAGNOSTIC REPORT`.

## 4. Risk-Based Verification Protocol
Provide evidence according to the change tier (Tier 1 Trivial ➔ Tier 4 Complex Flow). For UI changes, capture real screenshots with full Layout Shell. For User Flows or Performance improvements, include animated GIFs or screen recordings.
